// Expectation follows Linux v6.12 tcp_sequence (net/ipv4/tcp_input.c): the right edge RCV.NXT+RCV.WND is acceptable, so the RST draws a challenge ACK
// Upstream FreeBSD differs.
// Last ACK=11 and advertised window=32768 << 2 put the right edge at 131083.
// An RST there draws ACK=11; the RST at SEQ=10, below RCV.WUP=11, is dropped silently.
// The connection survives both RSTs: 10 more bytes echo. Handshake and
// scaled window: see handshake-linux-options.pkt and echo-and-close.pkt.

0     < S 0:0(0) win 64240 <mss 1460,nop,nop,sackOK,nop,wscale 7>
+0    > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,wscale 2,sackOK,eol,eol,eol>
+0    < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 502
+0    < P. 1:11(10) ack 1 win 502
+0    > P. 1:11(10) ack 11 win 32768
+0    < . 11:11(0) ack 11 win 502
+0    < R. 131083:131083(0) ack 11 win 0
+0    > . 11:11(0) ack 11 win 32768
+0    < R. 10:10(0) ack 11 win 0
+0.1  < P. 11:21(10) ack 11 win 502
+0    > P. 11:21(10) ack 21 win 32768
